    "model_design": "Change: Replace MolecularGNNEncoder with GraphTransformerEncoder (Category: Model Architecture). What: Replace the 3-layer GCN encoder with a graph transformer using multi-head attention (4 heads, 128 hidden dim) over the full adjacency, with a learnable global graph feature vector (CLS token) for improved graph-level representation. Additionally, fuse node features with fingerprints via a cross-attention layer before graph convolution. Why: ADMET properties depend on both local atomic environments and global molecular shape. Graph transformers with attention can capture long-range dependencies and learn multi-resolution features, while cross-attention fusion allows each node to attend to relevant fingerprint features (e.g., LogP, TPSA) for better context. This directly addresses the weak feature fusion and global pooling limitations. Implementation: Define GraphTransformerLayer with MultiheadAttention, LayerNorm, and FFN. In the encoder, first linearly project node features (74→128) and add a CLS token (learnable vector). Pass through 3 graph transformer layers that attend over the adjacency mask (full graph attention). For cross-modal fusion, project fingerprints (3239→128) and compute cross-attention between the CLS token and fingerprint representation, then concatenate to the CLS token. The final output is the CLS token fused with fingerprint info. Interface constraints: The forward method receives (node_features, adj_matrix, fingerprints) and returns a fused representation of shape (batch, hidden_dim). Must preserve variable names and output shape for compatibility with downstream MoE heads."
  }
}"}
